  "derivation": "Handwritten from the pinned Compendium only; no evaluator or implementation code was read or run. Level-one values are the reviewed v101 witnesses (re-checked: 21 starting Stamina + kit Stamina per echelon, human speed 5/stability 0, disengage 1 + kit bonus, Fury potency M-2/M-1/M). Each level from 2nd adds 9 Stamina (class/fury.md Basics); levels 1-3 are the 1st echelon (rule/general/echelon.md) so per-echelon kit Stamina does not change; Recoveries stay 10; recovery value = floor(max/3) (rule/health/recoveries.md) and winded = half of max rounded down (rule/health/winded.md + rule/general/always-round-down.md). No characteristic increase occurs before 4th level, so characteristics and potency are unchanged. Reaver speed adds Inescapable Wrath (bonus equal to Agility); Berserker stability at 3rd level adds Immovable Object (bonus equal to Might); bonuses add together (rule/dice/bonuses-and-penalties.md). Ability damage at Might 2 substitutes M=2 into printed tier text; the kit melee damage bonus is added per tier only for damage-dealing abilities with both Melee and Weapon keywords (chapter/kits.md Damage Bonuses). The level-2 aspect-ability option grouping is taken from the Heroes book because the unified file omits the lists; perk group membership is taken from the Heroes book Perks chapter headings and restricted to mcdm.heroes.v1 perks.",
